Work `.rptc/plans/unmeasured-fifth/overview.md` STEP 3 — DESIGN ONLY, change no tooling.

Every attribution failure found on 2026-09-07 came from one rule: a module is measured against
the suites that share its FILENAME (`focusModule.suitesFor`). Three shapes came out of it —
a suite scored against a module it never runs, a suite carrying a module's name that tests
something else, and a module tested only through a consumer's suite and so never measured.

WRITE A PROPOSAL at `.rptc/plans/unmeasured-fifth/attribution-design.md`. Do NOT change
focusModule.mjs, mutationScope.mjs, any config, or the baseline. This rule is what every
measurement in the repo rests on, and a wrong change still produces plausible numbers — the
owner decides this one awake.

The proposal must answer:
  - what attribution should key on instead. Stryker already computes which tests cover which
    mutants; the filename rule only decides which suites to RUN. Say whether that can be
    inverted and what it costs.
  - what a run costs under the new rule, measured or estimated with the arithmetic shown.
    Running every suite per module is correct and possibly unaffordable; say which.
  - how to PROVE the new set is right, including the control that would catch it being wrong.
  - what happens to the 628 baseline rows that exist — do they survive, need re-measuring,
    or change meaning?
  - what it does NOT fix. A module replaced everywhere by a jest.mock or an injected double
    is not an attribution problem and no rule change makes it measurable.

Two or three options with a recommendation, not a survey. Cite file:line for every claim
about how the current tooling behaves.

RAILS (the standing unattended contract). Stay on the work branch; never checkout or merge
develop. NO CLOUD WRITES and no live calls — tests and local measurement only. Commit only on
a GREEN check, exit codes captured in variables and never read through a pipe. Explicit
pathspec (`git commit -- <paths>`), never bare `git commit` or `-a`. `Backlog: PL-50` trailer.
No attribution trailers. If blocked, record what you learned and stop — do not force it.

CHECK before each commit: the suites you touched, `npx tsc --noEmit`, `npm run
typecheck:tests`, eslint on changed files, `npm run validate:test-file-sizes`.

FINISH with three or four plain sentences a tired reader understands: what you did, what you
found, what you did NOT do.
